    <othernotes>Wiz:

&lt;br&gt; A lich who, before becoming undead, was a powerful adventurer known by the moniker “Ice Witch”. She runs a magic item shop in the beginner town of Axel. Her store is usually filled with items either too expensive and high level for the starter town or items with significant drawbacks. Her potions and wares are mostly geared toward adventurers but she also stocks simpler items for the townsfolk, as well as incredibly niche items that never seem to sell.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
Personality:

&lt;br&gt; - Wiz is very meek and clumsy, and is always the first to apologize when something goes wrong, even if it’s not her fault. A stark contrast to how she was before becoming a lich, where she was headstrong and competitive. She is kind and well respected in Axel, and is taking her “life”… slower, and experiencing more since never taking the time to do so as a prominent adventurer. She gives off a gentle, older sister vibe.&lt;br&gt; 

- Despite having turned undead, Wiz possesses even more power than she did when she was alive, as she no longer has a limit to the amount of magical energy that her body can contain, unlike when she was human. She, however, hesitates to use such power because she knows how devastating it is, and will only use it under extreme conditions, or when innocent people are in danger. (To give you an idea of how much power she has, she too, can cast Explosion like Megumin, with over 3x the power, and can still move around with plenty of mana to spare.)&lt;br&gt; - 
Being a lich, the highest rank of undead, Wiz can’t die or age, per se, but she can be exorcised or destroyed. She fears moving on above all else, and will desperately plead if she is in danger of it, usually at the hands of Aqua. If she is near any kind of holy/sacred item, is hit by holy magic, or is hit by an extremely powerful spell/attack, she will start fading rapidly, and have almost no energy to move. She can only be restored with another’s vitality, or by a long period of rest away from holy power.&lt;br&gt; - Wiz has absolutely no business sense whatsoever. She often stocks items that are useful, but tend to have specific terrible drawbacks. She has yet to turn in a profit, leaving Vanir, also a fellow former Devil King general, to make all the money… which she ends up spending on more useless items to sell anyways. Vanir typically punishes her for this by forcing her to eat nothing but scraps, or zapping her to near oblivion.

&lt;br&gt; - She has come to the Inventory for a myriad of reasons, all of which Vanir told her to take advantage of so that she’d get out of the shop and fix her latest inventory blunder. These included meeting a great variety of new people, a chance at acquiring new business, and discovering an unexplored side of herself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Targetable traits:

&lt;br&gt; - Wiz is a powerful sorceress. She isn’t one to brag about her power, but doesn’t mind talking about it, while unintentionally telling how powerful she is. Contrary to being able to use the power to get whatever she wanted, she’ll usually submit and apologize rapidly.&lt;br&gt; 

- While she hides being undead from most people in her hometown, she's attempting to be more open about it here at the Inventory. She's still self-conscious, though, as she's used to people treating undead like they do monsters.&lt;br&gt; 

- Wiz won’t mind trying to talk business and other strategies, and she’ll need plenty of advice, considering she has none. She’ll also try selling her wares at times if one of items matches the need of another at the table.&lt;br&gt; - Being a shopkeeper Wiz is good at talking to her customers and other people about their problems and experiences, but she is somewhat shy about talking about herself.</othernotes>
